<title>SINGAPORE: Kian Ann builds new office for S$28 mln.</title>
<headline>Kian Ann builds new office for S$28 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kian Ann Engineering Ltd said Tuesday it plans to build new premises for Singapore $28 million to consolidate its office, warehousing and distribution operations.</p>
<p>The construction will be funded from internal resources and borrowings and the building is expected to be completed in the second half of 1998.</p>
<p>The engineering group also said it bought 75 percent of a Malaysian company Juta Tractors Enterprise Sdn Bhd for 375,000 Malaysian ringgit.</p>
<p>The principal activity of Juta is sourcing and distribution of an extensive range of machinery spares and diesel engine parts.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
